{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.carrier_gap_is_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.carrier_gap_is_three","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit.lean#L83-L88","doc":"The gap is exactly `3`, the distance between the identity's character and a\nthree-cycle's in `χ^{(2,1)}` — so the exclusion is a character-table fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.delta_L_is_not_a_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.delta_L_is_not_a_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**`Δ_L` is not a carrier**, and fails at order zero. A carrier needs\n`tr M(1) = 2`; the corpus's only elliptic operator — the only one clearing\nTIER-0 `D0` — gives `−1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.two_cos_two_pi_div_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.two_cos_two_pi_div_three","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit.lean#L68-L73","doc":"What `Δ_L` supplies instead: its classical eigenphase is exactly `2π/3`, and\n`2 cos (2π/3) = −1` — the `S₃` three-cycle's character. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.carrier_trace_at_classical_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.carrier_trace_at_classical_point","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The carrier's trace at the classical point. `α(1) = 0` because `α`'s `t¹`\ncoefficient is `z(1) − 1 = −1/2` in both conventions, so `tr M(1) = 2 cos 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.charpoly_of_trace_two_det_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.charpoly_of_trace_two_det_one","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseCarrierClassicalLimit.lean#L58-L61","doc":"With `tr M = 2` and `det M = 1` the characteristic polynomial is `(x−1)²`,\nso both eigenvalues are `1` and `M` is **unipotent**. ","signatureChunk":0}]}